From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Opsero <noreply@opsero.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: wilc1000: backport WILC3000 support (mainline
 v6.13..v6.18) to 6.12

The PYNQ-ZU carries a Microchip WILC3000 Wi-Fi/BT module on SDIO (PS SD1).
linux-xlnx 6.12.40 (AMD 2025.2) only knows the WILC1000: wilc_get_chipid()
rejects any chip ID that is not 0x1000xx, so the WILC3000 (0x3000xx) fails
at probe. Mainline added WILC3000 support in v6.13 (Marek Vasut / Ajay
Singh series "wifi: wilc1000: Add WILC3000 support"), plus follow-up fixes.

This patch replaces drivers/net/wireless/microchip/wilc1000 with the
mainline v6.15 driver, with these adjustments:
 - wlan_cfg.c/.h taken from v6.18 (bounds checks on firmware WID replies,
   "wifi: wilc1000: avoid buffer overflow in WID string configuration");
 - cfg80211 op signatures kept at their 6.12 form: set_monitor_channel()
   without the net_device argument (added in 6.13) and get_tx_power()
   without link_id (added in 6.14).
Included mainline changes: WILC3000 chip detection, SDIO/SPI register
differences, WILC3000 wake-up/sleep sequence, firmware name
atmel/wilc3000_wifi_firmware-1.bin, wiphy registration after chip ID read,
wiphy unregister on probe failure, error propagation from bus
acquire/release.

Compile-tested out-of-tree against linux-xlnx 6.12.40 (arm64, zynqmp).

Upstream-Status: Backport [mainline v6.13..v6.18, adapted to 6.12 cfg80211 API]
Signed-off-by: Opsero <noreply@opsero.com>
